#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119848 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119662 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d847ec9-c379-5013-ab77-a9b92dc8ca27" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Matrix With a Given Rank by Inspection"}] :question/id #uuid "a6a3db41-6033-537a-bc9d-03fde02dc869" :question/math-academy-id "e-5417" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices have a rank of $4?$\n\n![](images/2c/2cd43e61d4c51ee86d78217688daea5f8ebdfa656a9628e4bef3ef4ac9f8bd3a.svg)" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that a matrix of rank $4$ must have at least $4$ columns and at least $4$ rows. \nSo, we disregard the matrix $B$ since it has only $3$ rows. \n\nAlso, the matrix must have $4$ pivot columns. As we can see, the matrix $A$ has only $3$ pivot columns, while the matrix $C$ has exactly $4$ pivot columns. So, $\\textrm{rank}(A)=3$ and $\\textrm{rank}(C)=4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$C$ only\"."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d847ec9-c379-5013-ab77-a9b92dc8ca27" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120364 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d847ec9-c379-5013-ab77-a9b92dc8ca27" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Matrix With a Given Rank by Inspection"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "96575d6e-bf49-5dc7-8a78-535b3afb687b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118299} {:answer/id #uuid "ddbcd510-8196-5dd5-8040-8e0d74f88a8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "E = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118300} {:answer/id #uuid "e1dc381e-7fc9-51f4-91a7-448730b2123f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A = \\begin{bmatrix}5 & -3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 &